VALUES (626, '1', $t$ASK 626: a premise list written with bold or heading numbers is read, and a list the system cannot read is reported as LIST NOT READ, never as a forfeit$t$,
  $t$In run 42373 the defender's link round held six premises under its UNSUPPORTED-L4 PREMISES heading, numbered "**1.**" to "**6.**". Every item-head pattern wanted "1." followed by a space, so the list read as zero premises: the record said LINK ROUND FORFEITED, the judges were sent an empty ledger side, and two K-G10 items were sent to a judge against premises whose PRESSED WITH lines stood in the round text (WALL-11777 Finding 1 (a), (b), (c); W1, Wall 11804). This ASK makes every premise-list reader take one head form that accepts bold and heading numbers, and makes a list that is present but not read print LIST NOT READ, with no empty ledger, no K item and no count from it. Item 1(d), a set list form in the Oracle's prompt, was denied by the operator and is left out. (plan rev 1, ask626/w4/plan626.md md5 13acbe55; Wall 11822, 11812)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at about 04:57 to 04:59 CST 2026-11-25 on the operator's words "#626 doesn't require approval" (04:49 CST, as W4 cites them), and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11955, 11958; audit 42064). Engine 2df7f6fa to dc258730, 14 nodes, 423 nodes; the child aad0ad9c holds no list reader and was not written. What it does: one head form in every premise-list reader (optional "#" heading marks, bold marks, the number, "." or ")", optional closing bold, a space); a style lock (the first premise head sets the form of the list, and the premise count counts only heads of that form); a "### 1." item no longer ends a list body; a list with its heading present, text under it, zero premises read and no "PREMISE COUNT: 0", "none" or "no premises" line prints "LIST NOT READ: <side> -- the heading is present but the system read no premise under it; grade the list from the round text" in review_notes, the transcript and the judges' PRESSED-WITNESS LEDGER in place of LINK ROUND FORFEITED or an empty side; pwList returns null for it, so K-G10, K-P, K-R, the broken-press check, gate PL and prsUnprovenOnly raise nothing and no count comes from it. The LIST NOT READ line in the ledger is the one new text a judge sees (W1 N1); the judges' own FORFEIT rule text is untouched (W1 N2). IN PART, because it is shown offline only: t626 234 PASS, 0 FAIL with eight stored rounds; of 761 stored lists 758 read the same count and 3 change as intended (42373 e7f6922f and 42505 12957d6e, 0 to 6, bold; 42234 8dd067f4, 3 to 6, "###" with numbered lines inside premise 1); on 42373 the K-G10 items against the challenger go from 2 to 0. NOT SHOWN: no live run has gone through a bold or heading-numbered list; LIST NOT READ would print on none of the stored runs; the whole judgeBlock and ledger() of Panel Build and Build Independent Verdict were not run offline (their parts were). The grading: plan rev 0 PASS WITH N1, N2 (Wall 11824), applied in rev 1; build b1 FAIL on F1, the stored-rounds pass of the test had not been run (Wall 11918); regrade PASS WITH N3 after it ran (Wall 11928). N3: the six items-only changes on round d9924563 in the readers with no body-end stop are judged equal by rule, not by running their consumers, and the 761-list screen covered only the stop-bounded readers. Stated by W4 (Wall 11917, 11927): rev 0 had no style lock; a guard first put on LIB 998 was moved to 999; notes626.md first said d9924563 read byte-equal with the lock, which holds only for the stop-bounded readers. Open: two clean live runs in which a list path fires (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24); no revision of that is made by this row. REVISION (this row): the engine manual entry is WRITTEN, part 08.0 v299 to v320 (md5 e222253b, 52,600 characters), on the operator's press "Write it" at 05:14 CST 2026-11-25 on W3's card, and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11970, 11975). objective_met stays 'in part': no live run has gone through a list path.$t$,
  '11777, 11800, 11801, 11804, 11812, 11822, 11824, 11917, 11918, 11927, 11928, 11955, 11958, 11961, 11963, 11967, 11968, 11970, 11975',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), 220,
  to_jsonb($t$(1) Project chat, 18:07 CST 2026-11-24, on the WALL-11777 items: "1d. denied." (recorded by W3 at Wall 11812 and in md_notes_rulings of seat 33); the rest of ASK 626 was not touched by that ruling. (2) 21:01 CST 2026-11-24: "Build it" (as W4 cites it in notes626.md; W3 did not read the card or the message). (3) 04:49 CST 2026-11-25: "#626 doesn't require approval" (as W4 cites it at Wall 11955 and in audit_log row 42064; W3 did not read the message itself). W4 wrote on (3) with no write card pressed.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "#626 doesn't require approval", "question": "none: the write went on the operator's statement, not on a pressed card. W4 had posted a write card for ASK 626 at about 23:49 CST 2026-11-24 (Wall 11927); W3 does not know its id or whether it was pressed.", "thread": "W4", "press_time": "04:49 CST 2026-11-25 (the statement)", "build_approval": {"words": "Build it", "time": "21:01 CST 2026-11-24", "source": "notes626.md line 3 (W4). Not read by W3."}, "source": "Wall 11955; audit_log row 42064; Wall 11927. Not read by W3."}$j$::jsonb,
  'W4',
  $j${"md5": "13acbe55", "path": "ask626/w4/plan626.md", "note": "plan rev 1; rev 0 (342278b1, commit 876d56a5) graded PASS WITH N1, N2 by W1 (Wall 11824, commit 665492b1); rev 1 applies them by its own first line. No Wall grade of rev 1 by itself was found by W3.", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11822, 11824"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"md5": "424e3765", "path": "ask626/w4/b1/tg/target_engine_626.json", "note": "the engine target as written", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11917, 11928, 11955, 11958"}, {"md5": "d11525f0", "path": "ask626/w4/b1/b626.cjs", "note": "the build, rev 1 (rev 0 kept as b626_rev0.cjs 1a77a605)", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11917"}, {"md5": "f5560fa3", "path": "ask626/w4/b1/t626.cjs", "note": "the test as it stands after F1: it names each intended change and fails on any other (58ec7265 at the first build post, Wall 11917)", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11927"}, {"md5": "e166722b", "path": "ask626/w4/b1/fx/stored8.json", "note": "the stored-rounds fixture: 8 rows, 16 texts", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11927, 11928"}, {"md5": "df54fa79", "path": "ask626/w4/b1/tg/out_t626_stored.txt", "note": "test output with the stored rounds, 234 PASS, 0 FAIL (the count is from Wall 11927 and 11928; the file was not read by W3)", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "57d631e4", "path": "ask626/w4/b1/notes626.md", "note": "build notes with the residual on d9924563 (cf57df5d at the first build post)", "source": "md5sum and read whole by W3; Wall 11927"}, {"md5": "856c6515", "path": "ask626/w4/write/write626.sh", "note": "the write script (engine only)", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11955"}, {"md5": "97d11da2", "path": "ask626/w4/write/write626_run.txt", "note": "the write log: PUT engine http 200; dc258730-7f3a-4a5b-b53d-f38cd0355863 active, 423 nodes, params equal put, connections equal, changed the 14 nodes; child aad0ad9c unchanged; standing 31 PASS, 0 FAIL before and after; Library Check PASSES (lib 3cd2d095d2eb30eb, map 7d1a2893c4d1df8a)", "source": "md5sum and read (last lines) by W3"}, {"md5": "bfc4960e", "path": "ask626/w4/write/fetchback_eng_626.json", "note": "engine fetch-back after the write", "source": "md5sum by W3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"engine": {"path": "ask626/w4/write/revert_eng_626.json", "md5": "39df54a6", "note": "the engine before ASK 626 (2df7f6fa), made at the write"}, "child": "not written; nothing to revert", "database": "none: no database object was changed", "rehearsed": "not stated in the notes or the Wall posts W3 read", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11955; audit 42064"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1, N2 (plan rev 0)", "wall_id": 11824, "md5_graded": "342278b1", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11824; fairjudge/w1/g626/grade_plan626_r0.md (commit 665492b1)"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "FAIL, F1 (build b1: the stored-rounds pass of t626 named by plan C3 had not been run); the target reproduced as 424e3765", "wall_id": 11918, "md5_graded": "build b1 as first posted, before the stored-rounds pass was run (test t626.cjs 58ec7265, notes cf57df5d); the target itself did not change", "verdict_norm": "FAIL", "source": "Wall 11918; fairjudge/w1/g626/grade_build626_b1.md (commit 1ea292a6)"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N3 (build b1 regraded after F1: t626 with stored8.json 234 PASS, 0 FAIL on W1's run; the target is unchanged)", "wall_id": 11928, "md5_graded": "424e3765", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11928; fairjudge/w1/g626/grade_build626_b1.md (commit e063b64d)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['424e3765'], '[42064]'::jsonb,
  $j$[{"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "ORACLE_DEBATE_V1 (engine)", "before": "2df7f6fa", "after": "dc258730-7f3a-4a5b-b53d-f38cd0355863, active, 423 nodes; 14 nodes changed: D3 Build, C3 Build, C3 Extract, Build Independent Verdict, Build Save Body, Panel Build, Format Markdown, D4 Build, C4 Build, C2B Extract, D3B Extract, C3B Extract, Shared Library, Assume Check Build; 32 node lines and 9 Library lines tagged ASK 626; MAP n updated for 31 keys; Library sha 3cd2d095d2eb30eb, map 7d1a2893c4d1df8a"}, {"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "child", "before": "aad0ad9c", "after": "aad0ad9c, not written (it holds no list reader)"}, {"kind": "record and judge-facing text", "name": "LIST NOT READ line", "before": "LINK ROUND FORFEITED in review_notes and the transcript; an empty side in the judges' PRESSED-WITNESS LEDGER", "after": "\"LIST NOT READ: <side> -- the heading is present but the system read no premise under it; grade the list from the round text\" in the three places, when the heading is present and no premise is read; FORFEITED stays for a missing heading, \"PREMISE COUNT: 0\" or an empty list; the judges' own FORFEIT rule text unchanged"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"name": "t626.cjs with the stored rounds (fx/stored8.json: 12957d6e, 7124c5fb, 8dd067f4, b52fe836, d9924563, e7f6922f, efc9ff05, fd0edbff)", "result": "234 PASS, 0 FAIL by W4 and, identical, by W1. 256 reader runs: 202 byte-equal; 32 newly read, all intended (the \"**k.**\" lists of 42373 and 42505, live 0); 22 changed: 16 intended (42234 8dd067f4, 3 to 6, every reader) and 6 items-only with equal output (d9924563, the readers with no body-end stop). On 42373 [CR3]: live 0 premises, new 6; K-G10 on the challenger live 2, new 0; no FORFEITED line.", "source": "Wall 11917, 11927, 11928"}, {"name": "All stored lists (SQL screen)", "result": "761 lists; 758 read the same count; 3 change as intended. The screen emulated the stop-bounded readers only (W4's stated mistake, Wall 11927; W1 N3).", "source": "Wall 11917, 11927, 11928"}, {"name": "Standing set, Library Check pair, one-copy check", "result": "31 PASS, 0 FAIL; pair PASSES; one-copy PASS, at the build, before the PUT and on the fetch-back", "source": "Wall 11917, 11955; write626_run.txt 97d11da2"}, {"name": "NOT RUN", "result": "the whole judgeBlock and ledger() of Panel Build and Build Independent Verdict (their dependencies do not load offline); side(), sideLines and lnr626 were run by themselves", "source": "notes626.md; Wall 11918 (W1 N1 of the build grade)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "result": "MATCH (live engine dc258730 equals the graded target 424e3765 on every node's parameters and other fields; connections equal; 14 nodes changed against the base, none removed; child aad0ad9c unchanged; standing on live 31 PASS, 0 FAIL)", "wall_id": 11958, "source": "Wall 11958; fairjudge/w1/g626/readback_626.md (commit fb3bfbbe)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"case": "NO RUN YET. Shown offline on stored rounds only.", "runs": [], "mark_for_the_next_run": "a link round whose UNSUPPORTED-L4 PREMISES list is numbered in bold or with heading marks: the premise count read is the number of premises in the text, review_notes holds no LINK ROUND FORFEITED for that side, the judges' PRESSED-WITNESS LEDGER lists its pressed witnesses, and no K-G10 row names a witness that stands under the premise's PRESSED WITH line. A LIST NOT READ line, if one prints, is a reader failure to report at once with the round text. Two clean live runs in which a list path fires are owed.", "not_shown": "the judges' whole ledger block with the new readers; LIST NOT READ printed by a run; how a judge grades a list from the round text when the line prints.", "source": "notes626.md; Wall 11955, 11958"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"op_doc": "none", "engine_manual": "WRITTEN. Part 08.0 v299 (60734f59, 48,868 characters) to v320 (e222253b, 52,600): one new bullet, A PREMISE LIST THE SYSTEM CANNOT READ IS REPORTED, NEVER FORFEITED, after THE PRESSED-WITNESS LEDGER bullet; nothing deleted. Pairs manual1123/w3/a626/em_pairs_626_draft2.json (c0f785bf): draft 1 PASS WITH N1 (Wall 11963), draft 2 PASS (Wall 11968), both by W1. Operator's press \"Write it\" 05:14 CST 2026-11-25 on W3's card cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58XNrm4VgapADkJu2hTLoqx1. Written by W3 (Wall 11970); read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11975, commit f8704548)."}$j$::jsonb,
